#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# nand

#% text
# `nand(a, b, ...)` is `not (a and b and ...)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Arguments `true` are dropped; an argument `false` gives `true`; `nand()` is `false` and `nand(a)` is `not a`.

#% item
# Symbolic arguments otherwise stay.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
nand(true, false)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
nand(x, true, z)
#% output
#= nand(x, z)

#% cell
nand(x, false, z)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
nand(p, q)
#% output
#= nand(p, q)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `nor`, `and`, `not`, `xor`
